Show the account rate-limit budget (session + weekly) below the Claude sessions column in the --claude view.

DATA SOURCE (verified live, HTTP 200):
  GET https://api.anthropic.com/api/oauth/usage?at_wall=1&skip_spend=1
  Headers:
    Authorization: Bearer <token>
    anthropic-beta: oauth-2025-04-20
  Token: ~/.claude/.credentials.json -> claudeAiOauth.accessToken
         (siblings: refreshToken, expiresAt, subscriptionType, rateLimitTier)

RESPONSE SHAPE (real sample):
  five_hour.utilization = 13.0 (percent), five_hour.resets_at = ISO8601
  seven_day.utilization = 37.0 (percent), seven_day.resets_at = ISO8601
  limits: [ {kind:session|weekly_all|weekly_scoped, group, percent:int,
            severity:normal|..., resets_at:ISO8601, is_active:bool,
            scope:{model:{display_name}}|null} ]
  Prefer the limits[] array; fall back to five_hour/seven_day.
  session limit = 5h ; weekly limit = 7d (weekly_all).

CONSTRAINTS:
  - Render loop is ~1 fps: MUST NOT call the API per frame. Cache with a TTL
    (~60s) and fetch off the render thread (see _mem_cache / TTL in
    claude_sessions.py). ~1 request/min max.
  - Fail silent: network error / 401 / missing token / offline -> return None,
    panel keeps working, render nothing. Never crash the loop.
  - Do not attempt OAuth refresh. If accessToken expired (expiresAt in past), skip.
  - Gate on args.claude (only relevant in the sessions view).
  - Never log or expose the token.
  - Pure parse function (json dict -> dataclass) so tests use a captured fixture,
    no network in tests. Add the real sample as tests/fixtures.

RENDER: two compact rows under the sessions column, e.g.
  "Session 13%  resets 1h20m" / "Weekly 37%  resets 2d". Match render.py style;
  optionally tint by severity. Keep it small.

