Black text in the limit bars (Option B). render.py: text color INK->SURFACE (#0B0D12, the theme's near-black; no raw (0,0,0)). To keep black legible across the WHOLE bar - which the old accent-vs-dark-track split broke - the entire bar is now an accent chip: remaining budget = a lighter accent (new _mix(ACCENT,INK,0.34) helper, derived from theme tokens), consumed fraction = base ACCENT from the left. Both tones are light-accent (ACCENT is 7.7:1 vs SURFACE per theme.py), so SURFACE text reads over both the consumed and remaining segments; the used fraction is a tone shift rather than an empty-vs-filled contrast. Chose B over A (light full-width chip + accent segment) because a near-white INK chip would render two big white blocks in the footer - the accent chip stays on-brand and the fill still means something (bar = marker shape). Layout unchanged: two bars, full right half, percent left / reset right on one single-line-height bar, sessions full height, no waiting notice. 112 passed. Preview (scale=2, session 2% ~4h, weekly 37% ~3d): scratchpad/limits_black.png. Not verified: real-API data / on-hardware. No commit/tag.

